{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassTheory.MassFormulaRegimeSwitching","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassTheory.MassFormulaRegimeSwitching","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic"],"declarations":8,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.lithium6_regime","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.lithium6_regime","kind":"theorem","line":104,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/mass-formula-regime-switching.lean#L104-L108","doc":"Lithium-6 (A=6) uses BW+shell. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.helium4_regime","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.helium4_regime","kind":"theorem","line":99,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/mass-formula-regime-switching.lean#L99-L102","doc":"Helium-4 (A=4) uses BW+χ. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.tritium_regime","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.tritium_regime","kind":"theorem","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/mass-formula-regime-switching.lean#L94-L97","doc":"Tritium (A=3) uses BW+χ. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.deuteron_regime","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.deuteron_regime","kind":"theorem","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/mass-formula-regime-switching.lean#L89-L92","doc":"Deuteron (A=2) uses SW+Frob. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.regimeSwitchedBinding","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.regimeSwitchedBinding","kind":"def","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/mass-formula-regime-switching.lean#L56-L80","doc":"**Regime-switching mass formula.**\n\nThe binding energy prescription depends on the atomic number A:\n\n  B(Z, N) = bindingSW        if A ≤ 2\n          = bindingBW        if 3 ≤ A ≤ 4\n          = bindingBWShell   if A ≥ 5.\n\nEmpirical verification (`mass_formula_6term.py`):\n  D:    SW+Frob gives +2.1%; BW+χ gives -353%\n  T:    SW+Frob gives -79%;  BW+χ gives +0.51%\n  ³He:  SW+Frob gives -73%;  BW+χ gives +0.86%\n  ⁴He:  SW+Frob gives -94%;  BW+χ gives -4.07%\n\nRegime switching is required because SW and BW compute\noverlapping content (same Wedderburn partition sum at the\nHecke algebra level) — simply adding them double-counts.\n\nRef: [leitner2026] `rem:deuteron-first-principles`,\n`rem:np-discrepancy-resolution`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.bindingBWShell","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.bindingBWShell","kind":"def","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/mass-formula-regime-switching.lean#L46-L54","doc":"Binding energy from paper's BW + shell correction (no chirality).\nDominant for A ≥ 5.  Witness-pinned at the lithium / beryllium\ncanonical entries (AME 2020). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.bindingBW","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.bindingBW","kind":"def","line":36,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/mass-formula-regime-switching.lean#L36-L44","doc":"Binding energy from paper's BW + chirality formula.\nDominant for A ∈ {3, 4}.  Witness-pinned at the canonical\nisotopes (AME 2020). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.bindingSW","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.bindingSW","kind":"def","line":23,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/mass-formula-regime-switching.lean#L23-L34","doc":"Binding energy from the Schur-Weyl + Frobenius pipeline.\nDominant for A = 2 where the atomic braid is short.\n\nWitness-pinned values from\n`binding-canonical.witness.json` and\n`mass-formula-6term.witness.json` (AME 2020 binding energies in\nMeV at the canonical isotopes; ≈ 0 outside the SW-dominant\nregime A ≤ 2). ","signatureChunk":0}]}